# --- s036 Book I d.8 q.4 = Ord. I d.8 p.1 q.4 (Vat. IV)
n("n606","s036-01","Quarta questio octaue distinctionis","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 4, *utrum cum simplicitate divina possit stare distinctio perfectionum essentialium praecedens omnem actum intellectus*. This is the *locus classicus* of the formal distinction (*distinctio formalis a parte rei*). Gorris's *aliquo modo* differs from the Vatican wording (*omnem actum*?); to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n607","s036-01","Ad oppositum est Dionisius","la","source","Ps.-Dionysius, *De divinis nominibus* (c. 5 or c. 13 in the Latin versions), on the unity of the divine perfections. The exact wording *multiplex formatio… est unita* has not been identified.","to-verify")
n("n608","s036-02","opinio Thome primo scripti dist. 2.","la","source","Aquinas, *Scriptum super Sent.* I d. 2 q. 1 a. 2–3: the attributes differ *ratione*, the *ratio* being in our intellect though founded in God.","to-verify")
n("n609","s036-02","Eruey","la","historical","Hervaeus Natalis OP (d. 1323), whose *In I Sent.* d. 2 on the distinction of the divine attributes is meant. The form printed is *Eruey* (genitive?). This is a later author than Scotus, adduced by Gorris.","to-verify")
n("n610","s036-02","inquiunt","la","textual","*inquiunt* (plural: ‘they say’), referring to Thomas and Hervaeus together. As printed.")
n("n611","s036-02","Godofredus quodlibeto. 7°. q. 1.","la","source","Godfrey of Fontaines, *Quodl.* VII q. 1 (on the distinction of the divine attributes). To be checked against the Vatican apparatus to *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 4.","to-verify")
n("n612","s036-02","quodlibeto. 5. q. 1. et quodlibeto. 13. q. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* V q. 1 (the attributes distinguished by the act of the divine intellect), and *Quodl.* XIII q. 1 (?). The second reference is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n613","s036-02","in summa articulo. 37. q. 7.","la","source","Henry, *Summa* a. 37 (?) q. 7. Henry's treatment of the attributes falls in *Summa* aa. 32–75. The precise article is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n614","s036-04","vnitas capitur quadrupliciter","la","source","Gorris's four grades of unity (aggregation, order, composition, indivision) are a compressed version of Scotus's scale of unity. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 2 p. 2 qq. 1–4 n. 403 and *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 4: *unitas aggregationis, ordinis, per accidens, per se compositi, simplicitatis*.","to-verify")
n("n615","s036-05","non est ydemptitas et distinctio","la","textual","The fifth conclusion is hard to construe as printed (*ad attributa non est ydemptitas et distinctio*). The sense seems to be that the supreme unity of the essence excludes a real distinction of the attributes, but not their formal non-identity. Not checked against B.","uncertain")
n("n616","s036-06","attributa habent non ydemptitatem preter intellectum","la","source","Scotus's thesis: the attributes are formally non-identical *ex natura rei*, prior to any act of the intellect. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 4 nn. 192–193 (*non-identitas formalis*).","to-verify")
n("n617","s036-04","war","en","translation","*bellum* … *ad ducem*: Aristotle's image of the army ordered to its general (*Metaph.* XII 10, 1075a13–15), here as *bellum*.")
n("n618","s036-05","in their formal","en","translation","*rationes formales* is left half-untranslated: the formal ‘notions’ or ‘definitions’ of the attributes.")

# --- B collation (full): B51L–B52L
n("n964","s036-02","quodlibeto. 5°. q. 3.","la","textual","B: *quolib. iij. q. iij.* (B checked).","certain")
n("n965","s036-05","vnitate essentie ad attributa","la","textual","B: *vnitate essentie cum attributis*.","certain")
upd("n615", text="The fifth conclusion is hard to construe as printed (*ad attributa non est ydemptitas et distinctio*). B reads *cum summa vnitate essentie cum attributis non est identitas et distinctio*, which is easier: there is no identity-with-distinction of the essence with the attributes that conflicts with supreme unity. The sense seems to be that the supreme unity of the essence excludes a real distinction of the attributes, but not their formal non-identity. B does not remove the difficulty of *non est*.")
